# ⚠️⚠️⚠️ NEVER POINT THIS AT PRODUCTION NEON ⚠️⚠️⚠️
# The value below must be a DEDICATED Neon branch (e.g. a `dev` branch created
# from `main` in the Neon console), NEVER the production branch `main`.
# Local test runs perform destructive operations (migrate down / re-seed) that
# would wipe production data. See ADR-0012 (adrs/0012-separacion-dev-prod-db.md)
# and DEPLOY-PLAN.md ("Flujo de desarrollo local").
#
# This file is documentation only: no dotenv dependency, nothing is auto-loaded.
# Set the environment variable yourself before running migrations or the seed:
#
#   PowerShell:  $env:DATABASE_URL = "postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
#   bash/zsh:    export DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
#
# Example Neon connection string (dev branch, NOT production):
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@ep-xxxx-dev.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
# CORS_ORIGIN restricts the REST API + Socket.IO to a single trusted origin.
# Optional: unset locally, so dev/tests stay permissive (defaults to "*").
# In production (Render), set it to the deployed Vercel frontend URL:
#   CORS_ORIGIN=https://pokeduels.vercel.app
# PORT is the HTTP listener port (Render injects its own; default 3000):
#   PORT=3000
# LOG_LEVEL gates pino output (default "info"; "debug"/"trace" for local dev):
#   LOG_LEVEL=info
# Pool tuning (backend/db/pool.js — all optional, these are the defaults):
#   PG_POOL_MAX=10
#   PG_POOL_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
#   PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Destructive-op guard for the test bootstrap (backend/test/helpers.js):
# set to 1 ONLY when DATABASE_URL points at a throwaway DB (a Neon dev branch
# or CI's ephemeral branch) — see ADR-0012:
#   ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB_TESTS=0